{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Load your level and catalogs, construct horizontal ground, and follow a character"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"horizontally, vertically, or in all 2D directions with reusable API helpers."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Assemble Levels, Construct Ground, and Follow Targets","modules":[{"name":"Scroller2d"}]},"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/DecisionPoint","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/AppSharedSceneBaseLifecycle","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/ManagedCallbacks","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/BaseClasses","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/BaseTypeStructure","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/SharedObjects","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Configuration","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Extensions","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Enumerations","doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Other"],"anchor":"Essentials","title":"Essentials","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/LevelHelpers"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Supported-directions","text":"Supported directions","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each helper has its own scope:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Helper"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Direction support"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LevelAssemblyHelper.Resources"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Loads level and catalog models independently of camera-follow direction."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LevelAssemblyHelper.build"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Assembles horizontal levels; requires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scrollOrientation"},{"type":"text","text":" to be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"horizontal\""},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CreateGroundHelper"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Constructs flat horizontal terrain and gaps."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CameraFollowHelper"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Follows horizontally, vertically, or on both axes independently of the assembly and ground helpers."}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use the camera helper independently in a vertical-scrolling or free-moving"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2D game with your own scene and terrain construction."}]},{"text":"Load and assemble","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Load-and-assemble"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call these helpers on the main actor, after configuring the SDK’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runningDevice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defaultDevice"},{"type":"text","text":" for your game. URLs may come from your app bundle or workspace."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The level file uses the existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SceneConfig"},{"type":"text","text":" format. Obstacle and character catalogs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObstacleConfig"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CharacterConfig"},{"type":"text","text":"; the object catalog is an array of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GenericObject"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"code":["let resources = try LevelAssemblyHelper.Resources(","    levelURL: levelURL,","    obstacleURL: obstacleURL,","    characterURL: characterURL,","    objectURL: objectURL",")","let result = try LevelAssemblyHelper.build(","    resources: resources,","    scene: self,","    groundTexture: { name in SKTexture(imageNamed: name) }",")","result.install(in: self)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppSharedSceneBase"},{"type":"text","text":". The result exposes the world root, ground geometry,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"obstacle nodes, and character nodes. Installing applies scene size, anchor point, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scale mode, attaches the root, and commits the ground lookup and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"levelEndPoint"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Remove the previous result’s root before installing a different level.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Catalog properties supply defaults. Non-nil per-level properties override them, nested","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties merge, and device records merge by their exact ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceName","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" string. An explicit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty array clears a catalog array. Missing definitions and decoding failures throw.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Assembly uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"CreateObstacleHelper","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"CreateCharacterHelper","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", retaining the existing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SDK animation, physics, and behavior. Their image names must resolve through the scene’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"normal texture cache and bundled assets. ","type":"text"},{"code":"groundTexture","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" resolves terrain only and can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"map editor names to namespaced asset catalog names. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"configureObstacle"},{"text":" to adjust","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resolved obstacle properties before construction.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default character factory produces the SDK’s enemy node class. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"createCharacter"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"to customize or skip individual characters. Add your player, backgrounds, coins, artifacts,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checkpoints, and end triggers through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"addContent"},{"text":", which receives the loaded resources,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world root, and ground result. These callbacks are synchronous and may throw. Assembly","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"temporarily attaches its root so the existing scene-coordinate conversion helpers work,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then detaches it before returning. It restores the previous ground lookup and end point","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on success or failure. Keep callback side effects within the supplied root.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Input, collision responses, collection rules, checkpoint state, victory UI, and replay","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remain game-specific. Assembly does not automatically install scene\/contact delegates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Construct-ground-independently","text":"Construct ground independently","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let terrain = try CreateGroundHelper(","    sections: resources.level.ground ?? [],","    origin: CGPoint(x: -437, y: -201),","    texture: { SKTexture(imageNamed: $0) }",")","addChild(terrain.root)","terrain.installGroundLookup(in: self)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The builder supports horizontal ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Ground"},{"text":" sections, optional bottom-layer tiles,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"repeat counts, device sizes and offsets, anchors, z positions, and gap materials.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An optional ","type":"text"},{"code":"collisionTopInset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lowers the collision surface without resizing artwork;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assembly exposes the same setting as ","type":"text"},{"code":"groundCollisionTopInset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Adjacent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"surfaces with matching geometry and collision masks share a static collision body.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Set masks per section in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/GroundSection\/collisionMasks","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Returned surfaces describe","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the full collision rectangles; the SDK ground lookup stores their top edges. ","type":"text"},{"code":"bounds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"includes horizontal gaps, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"endPoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the ground cursor at the baseline.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use identity transforms for the world and terrain roots so the lookup remains in scene","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"coordinates. For stacked terrain, list the images in bottom-to-top order in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"image"},{"text":" and set ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stack"},{"text":" to true. The first column is always present and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"repeatCount"},{"text":" adds more columns. On unstacked terrain, a repeat count of zero","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uses one tile.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"groundPhysicsAngleType"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"angle"},{"text":" to derive collision from tile","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"textures, or use the edge flags to add beveled ends, vertical edges, or a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lower floor. The ground lookup still records one top height per section for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"object placement. The collision geometry handles traversal over the slope.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gap"},{"text":" for water, lava, fire, or other artwork between ground sections. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"distance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" width moves the terrain cursor and its height sets the height of each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tile. A zero height uses the device tile height or source texture height.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Tile width comes from the device size or the source texture. The builder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"repeats whole tiles across the gap. The device offset positions the artwork,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a negative X offset lets it extend under the terrain on the left. Overlap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also extends to the right when a whole tile exceeds the opening. The material"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"draws beneath overlapping ground. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"None"},{"type":"text","text":" with a width for an empty span. Gap materials have no floor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collision. Add a game-specific sensor if contact should trigger swimming or damage."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a static fill, set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" to a texture name. For waves or flicker, set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" to a sprite atlas name and set the section’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"animation"},{"type":"text","text":" dictionary."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/GroundSection"},{"type":"text","text":" for a two-frame example. The optional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gapAnimationTextures"},{"type":"text","text":" resolver can supply ordered frames from a custom asset store."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bounds describe terrain, so extend them for any playable area beyond it."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Follow-a-target-horizontally-vertically-or-in-all-2D-directions","text":"Follow a target horizontally, vertically, or in all 2D directions","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CameraFollowHelper"},{"type":"text","text":" supports independent horizontal and vertical axis controls."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Horizontal following is enabled by default, and vertical following is disabled."}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Follow mode"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"followsHorizontal"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"followsVertical"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Horizontal (default)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertical"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All 2D directions"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Neither axis"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A disabled axis retains the camera’s existing position. Enabling both axes follows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any combination of horizontal, vertical, and diagonal target movement; it does not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rotate the camera or automatically change zoom."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Retain the helper as a scene property and update it after physics. This example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"follows the target on both axes:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let follow = CameraFollowHelper(","    camera: cameraNode,","    target: hero,","    viewportSize: visibleWorldSize,","    bounds: playableBounds",")","follow.followsHorizontal = true","follow.followsVertical = true","follow.lookAhead = .zero","follow.smoothing = 8","","\/\/ From the scene's didSimulatePhysics hook:","follow.update(deltaTime: frameDelta)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For vertical-only following, set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"followsHorizontal = false"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"followsVertical = true"},{"type":"text","text":". For horizontal-only following, use the defaults."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Smoothing and look-ahead work on each enabled axis. Smoothing is an exponential"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"response per second; zero snaps immediately. Set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lookAhead.dx"},{"type":"text","text":" for a horizontal"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offset and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lookAhead.dy"},{"type":"text","text":" for a vertical offset. These offsets are fixed in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"camera-parent coordinates; they do not automatically reverse with target movement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Optional "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" constrain each enabled axis and use camera-parent coordinates."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A world smaller than the viewport centers on that axis. Supply bounds covering the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full playable height for vertical or all-direction following. Terrain-only bounds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that are no taller than the viewport prevent vertical travel even when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"followsVertical"},{"type":"text","text":" is enabled. Set "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bounds = nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for unrestricted following. Update "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"viewportSize"},{"type":"text","text":" when the view, scale mode, or camera zoom changes;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it must describe the visible world dimensions, rather than screen pixels. Keep the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"camera unrotated. The helper handles target coordinate conversion, weak references,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"invalid frame deltas, and targets removed from the scene. Reset your frame timer after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pausing to avoid a large resume delta."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/scroller2d\/levelhelpers"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/ManagedCallbacks":{"title":"How does Scroller2d manage callbacks","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deciding to use the game object helpers or roll your own."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/ManagedCallbacks","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/managedcallbacks"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/DecisionPoint":{"title":"Decision Point","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Deciding to use the game object helpers or roll your own."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/DecisionPoint","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/decisionpoint"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/GroundSection/collisionMasks":{"type":"topic","title":"collisionMasks","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The category, collision, and contact masks for a solid ground section."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/GroundSection\/collisionMasks","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"collisionMasks"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Scroller2d18CollisionDetectionV","text":"CollisionDetection"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/groundsection\/collisionmasks","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/BaseTypeStructure":{"title":"Base Structure","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the core data types that define levels, scenes, and gameplay objects."}],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/BaseTypeStructure","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/basetypestructure"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/Other":{"title":"Other","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the core data types that define levels, scenes, and gameplay objects."}],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Other","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/other"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/AppSharedSceneBaseLifecycle":{"title":"AppSharedSceneBase Lifecycle","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"When using "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/AppSharedSceneBase"},{"type":"text","text":" how does Scroller2d provide feedback to my code."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/AppSharedSceneBaseLifecycle","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/appsharedscenebaselifecycle"},"appicon.png":{"identifier":"appicon.png","alt":"Scroller2d","variants":[{"url":"\/images\/Scroller2d\/appicon.png","traits":["1x","light"]}],"type":"image"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/SharedObjects":{"title":"Shared Structures","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the core data types that define levels, scenes, and gameplay objects."}],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/SharedObjects","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/sharedobjects"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/Extensions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Extensions","role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/extensions","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Browse the core data types that define levels, scenes, and gameplay objects."}],"kind":"article","title":"Extensions","type":"topic"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/Configuration":{"title":"Configuration","abstract":[{"text":"Browse the core data types that define levels, scenes, and gameplay objects.","type":"text"}],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Configuration","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/configuration"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/GettingStarted":{"title":"Getting Started with Scroller2d","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a level and assign background and ground elements."}],"role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/GettingStarted","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/gettingstarted"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/GroundSection":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/GroundSection","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GroundSection"}],"url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/groundsection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"GroundSection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A structure representing all the properties and types needed to create a specific horizontal ground section."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GroundSection"}]},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d":{"abstract":[{"text":"Scroller2d is an api interface and visual editor that allows a developer to quickly create 2d SpriteKit games with minimal effort.","type":"text"}],"title":"Scroller2d","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d","type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d","images":[{"type":"icon","identifier":"appicon.png"}]},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/Enumerations":{"title":"Enumerations","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/Enumerations","type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"text":"Browse the core data types that define levels, scenes, and gameplay objects.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/enumerations"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/BaseClasses":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"Base Classes","url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/baseclasses","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/BaseClasses","kind":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Browse the core data types that define levels, scenes, and gameplay objects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Scroller2d/documentation/Scroller2d/AppSharedSceneBase":{"title":"AppSharedSceneBase","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The base SKScene implementation for Scroller2d."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"AppSharedSceneBase","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Scroller2d\/documentation\/Scroller2d\/AppSharedSceneBase","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AppSharedSceneBase","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/scroller2d\/appsharedscenebase"}}}